[size=2][color=#9a9a9a]Crusader Kings III 1.19  |  UI mod  |  Save-game safe  |  Ironman friendly  |  English & Portuguese (BR)[/color][/size][/center]

[line]

[center][size=4][b][color=#d4af37]Stop guessing who should raise your heir[/color][/b][/size][/center]

Picking a guardian in vanilla means eyeballing skills and hoping. [b]GCA[/b] puts a number on every candidate: the actual chance that the child gains education progress with that guardian, computed with [b]the same formula the game uses[/b]. No rules are changed. You just finally see the odds.

[center][size=5][b][color=#7fc8f8]GCA 68%  ~R3[/color][/b][/size]
[size=2][color=#9a9a9a]68% chance of +2 education points every birthday  |  projected rank 3 at adulthood[/color][/size][/center]

[line]

[center][size=4][b][color=#d4af37]A real score on every candidate[/color][/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sujirodev/ck3-guardian-calc-assistant/main/docs/images/feature_score.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[*]Shown in [b]Educate Child[/b], [b]Offer Guardianship[/b] and [b]Offer Ward[/b].
[*]Works both ways: rate guardians for a child, or children for a guardian.
[*]Hover for the full breakdown: every factor, the point projection and the notes that apply to the pair.
[*]Smart notes: Beacon of Learning, Pedagogy, commander trait transfer, Knighthood, different faith or culture.
[/list]

[line]

[center][size=4][b][color=#d4af37]Find guardians beyond your court[/color][/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sujirodev/ck3-guardian-calc-assistant/main/docs/images/feature_search.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[*]New [b]Find Guardian (GCA)[/b] interaction on any child at your court without a guardian.
[*]Searches your court [b]and every court in your diplomatic range[/b].
[*]Opens sorted with the [b]best guardian on top[/b]. [i]GCA: by score[/i] and [i]Default list[/i] buttons sit under the native sort dropdown.
[*][b]Quick / Intelligent / Genius[/b] filter, plus the native [i]Traits[/i] filter.
[*]Pick someone and click [i]Continue[/i]: [i]Educate Child[/i] (your court) or [i]Offer Ward[/i] (foreign court) opens already filled in. Vanilla costs and acceptance apply.
[/list]

[line]

[center][size=4][b][color=#d4af37]Why trust the number?[/color][/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sujirodev/ck3-guardian-calc-assistant/main/docs/images/feature_formula.png[/img][/center]

GCA mirrors the vanilla education roll that runs on every birthday from 6 to 15, and reads the game's own factors, so overhaul mods that retune them are followed automatically.

[spoiler]
[b]Vanilla quirks kept as they are[/b]
[list]
[*]Cultures with "better ward education" (Storytellers and similar) [i]replace[/i] the guardian's intellect and skill bonus with a flat +10. GCA reproduces this and warns you.
[*]No focus yet: the guardian's best skill is assumed.
[*]Projected rank uses the vanilla cut-offs (7 / 12 / 17 points). ~R4 means rank 4 or 5.
[*]Beacon of Learning adds round(points / 4), up to +3, at coming of age; it is included in the projection.
[*]The projection only counts the birthday rolls. Events, court tutors and universities can add more.
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[line]

[center][size=4][b][color=#d4af37]Installation[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[list=1]
[*]Download the zip from the [b]Files[/b] tab.
[*]Extract it into [i]Documents/Paradox Interactive/Crusader Kings III/mod/[/i]. You should see [i]guardian_calc_assistant.mod[/i] next to the [i]guardian_calc_assistant[/i] folder.
[*]Enable it in the launcher.
[/list]

Safe to add to or remove from an existing save.

[line]

[center][size=4][b][color=#d4af37]Compatibility[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Game version:[/b] 1.19
[*][b]Overrides:[/b] [i]gui/interaction_confirmation.gui[/i]. Conflicts with other mods that override that same file.
[*][b]Marriage Calculation Assistant:[/b] compatible.
[*]The list row inherits whatever row your playset uses, so other UI mods' tweaks are kept.
[*][b]Portuguese (BR)[/b] shows when the game runs with the community PT-BR translation (which adds that language). Everyone else gets English.
[/list]

